{%- set land_prompt %}<<cfg.default_prompt('merge-pr', '${{ matrix.pr }}')>>

tend-land: every check on ${{ needs.check.outputs.sha }} has finished green, the head a review recorded for landing (`tend/land/${{ matrix.pr }}`). Complete the landing decision for that exact head. The review's CI wait is off (`await_ci: false`).{% endset -%}
{%- set repair_prompt %}<<cfg.default_prompt('continue-pr', '${{ matrix.pr }}')>>

CI settled red on this PR's head ${{ needs.check.outputs.sha }} after its review ended. The review's CI wait is off (`await_ci: false`).{% endset -%}
{%- set current = "steps.current.outputs.current == 'true'" -%}
{#- Reads whether the head a session was started for is still the PR's, so a
    session queued behind another that already moved the head ends before
    `setup:` and the agent cost anything. #}
{%- macro still_current() %}
      - name: Check the head is still the PR's
        id: current
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
          PR: ${{ matrix.pr }}
          SHA: ${{ needs.check.outputs.sha }}
        run: |
          tend runtime current-head
{%- endmacro -%}
<<header>>
name: tend-land
# Lands a reviewed PR once its CI completes, with no session waiting for it.
# With the review's CI wait off, a review that settles everything about a head
# the bot pushed but its CI records the head for landing (a `tend/land/<PR>`
# commit status naming the base and any skipped checks) and ends. `check`, Tend's
# pinned script with no agent and no checkout of the PR, runs whenever anything
# that reports on a commit finishes, so whatever its gate waits on also wakes
# it: every workflow but Tend's own, a commit status, or another app's check
# suite. It decides only what is crisp: a record for that head and base, and
# every check finished. Green with a record starts a short `land` session per
# PR that makes the landing decision; a red on a PR with no human author starts
# `repair`. `land_pr.py` documents the records.
on:
  workflow_run:
    workflows: ["**", "!tend-*"]
    types: [completed]
  status:
  check_suite:
    types: [completed]

jobs:
  check:
    # Filtered here, before a runner is allocated, so the wake-up costs
    # nothing for events that can't land or repair anything: a pending status;
    # Tend's own push and repair markers, which change no verdict; a workflow
    # run or check suite with no PR in this repository behind it (a push to
    # this repo's default branch or to a branch with no PR). A fork PR's run
    # lists no PR either, so a run from another repository passes.
    if: >-
      <<fork_guard_prefix(cfg)>><<tend_enabled>> && (
        (github.event_name == 'status'
          && github.event.state != 'pending'
          && github.event.context != 'tend/land/pushed'
          && github.event.context != 'tend/land/repair')
        || (github.event_name == 'workflow_run'
          && (github.event.workflow_run.pull_requests[0] != null
            || github.event.workflow_run.head_repository.full_name != github.repository))
        || (github.event_name == 'check_suite'
          && github.event.check_suite.pull_requests[0] != null))
    # One check per commit at a time: a burst of events for one head runs the
    # first and the newest, which re-reads everything the others would have.
    concurrency:
      group: ${{ github.workflow }}-check-${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_sha || github.event.check_suite.head_sha || github.event.sha }}
      cancel-in-progress: false
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
<<environment()>>
    permissions:
      contents: read
    outputs:
      sha: ${{ steps.event.outputs.sha }}
      land_prs: ${{ steps.check.outputs.land_prs }}
      red_prs: ${{ steps.check.outputs.red_prs }}
    steps:
<<setup_tend_runtime()>>
      - name: Read the event's commit
        id: event
        env:
          SHA: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.head_sha || github.event.check_suite.head_sha || github.event.sha }}
        run: echo "sha=$SHA" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
      - uses: max-sixty/tend/land@<<tend_version>>
        id: check
        with:
          github_token: ${{ secrets.<<bot_token_secret>> }}
          head_sha: ${{ steps.event.outputs.sha }}

  # One session per PR. Each shares the review's concurrency group for that
  # PR, so a landing or repair never runs beside a review of the same PR, and
  # queues rather than replacing a pending one.
  land:
    needs: check
    if: needs.check.outputs.land_prs != '[]' && needs.check.outputs.land_prs != ''
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        pr: ${{ fromJSON(needs.check.outputs.land_prs) }}
    # The job's name carries its PR, which is how `active_subject_runs.py`
    # finds this session as the PR's owner.
    name: "land #${{ matrix.pr }}"
    concurrency:
      group: tend-review-${{ matrix.pr }}
      queue: max
      cancel-in-progress: false
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
<<environment()>>
    permissions:
<<permissions()>>
    steps:
<<setup_tend_runtime()>>
<<still_current()>>
<<checkout(cfg, ref=cfg.default_branch, if_condition=current)>>
<<agent_step(cfg, block_input('prompt', land_prompt), if_condition=current)>>

  # A PR with no human author went red after its review ended, so no session
  # is waiting to repair it; this one continues it, as the review would have.
  repair:
    needs: check
    if: needs.check.outputs.red_prs != '[]' && needs.check.outputs.red_prs != ''
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        pr: ${{ fromJSON(needs.check.outputs.red_prs) }}
    name: "repair #${{ matrix.pr }}"
    concurrency:
      group: tend-review-${{ matrix.pr }}
      queue: max
      cancel-in-progress: false
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
<<environment()>>
    permissions:
<<permissions()>>
    steps:
<<setup_tend_runtime()>>
<<still_current()>>
<<checkout(cfg, ref=cfg.default_branch, if_condition=current)>>
<<setup_current>>
<<agent_step(cfg, block_input('prompt', repair_prompt), if_condition=current)>>
